Subject: [PATCH 13/15] [ExpressionLanguage] Bound the nesting level of parsed
 expressions

The parser stacks one node per nesting level with no limit, so a short crafted
expression builds a node tree tens of thousands of levels deep. Destroying that
tree recurses on the native stack and segfaults the process, before anything is
evaluated. Count the nodes stacked on the branch being built and reject too
deeply nested expressions with a catchable SyntaxError instead.

The nesting level misses the levels that a chain of binary operators or of
property accesses adds above its first operand, so the depth of the node tree
is also checked once parsed.

